  "historical_record": [
    {
      "date": "1973-04-12",
      "kind": "planning decision",
      "description": "Lot 66 in Block 5872, at the southwest corner of Trumbull Street and Alemany Boulevard, was a 1,500-square-foot R-1 lot almost entirely covered by an existing dwelling, beside about 350 square feet of unused street land kept as outdoor space. The City Planning Commission unanimously found in conformity with the Master Plan the vacation of unused portions of Trumbull Street and Alemany Boulevard next to Lot 66, Block 5872, so the land could be sold and added to that lot.",
